in-place: left part is always sorted right part is not. go from left to right picking elements and "inserting" them 
into their correct place on the left side.

Runtime is O(n^2) because each insertion requires searching left completely worst case and there is a right shift.


CODE: (my own and not from Cormen .. :-))

for (i = 1; i < a->length; i++) {
    const int value = a[i];
    int counter     = 0;

    while(counter < i && a[counter] < value) { 
        counter++;
    }

    if (counter != i) {
       rightRotate(a, ctr, a->length - 1);   // rightRotate(array, start, end)
       swap(a, ctr, i++)'
    }
}

